# Editor backups
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# Local config (don't commit secrets / per-user paths)
.env
.env.local

# Node data directory (default data_dir; UUID-named db/table folders + JSONL)
/zetta-data/

# Python tooling (scripts/ generators; run via `uv run` — deps are PEP 723 inline)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Generated training-data corpus (docs/agent/training-data-runbook.md). Root-level outputs
# are SCRATCH — ignored; the tracked, committed corpora live in data/ (see data/README.md).
# Root-anchored so both data/*.jsonl and the test fixtures (tests/fixtures/*.jsonl) stay tracked.
/corpus.jsonl
/corpus*.jsonl

/autosuggest.jsonl
/autosuggest*.jsonl

# Trained checkpoints — large (~GBs); kept local and pushed to a private HF model repo,
# never committed. The training-metrics log lives alongside (data/checkpoints/*/train.log).
/data/checkpoints/
# Training corpora live on the Hub, NOT in git and NOT merely regenerated.
#
#   https://huggingface.co/datasets/OramaSearch/base-agent-interaction-corpus  (private)
#
# They were ignored on the grounds of being "reproducible from the native generator". That is false
# the moment the generator changes — and it changed a dozen times in a day, so regenerating from a
# later commit yields a DIFFERENT corpus. A checkpoint whose corpus was not kept cannot be
# reproduced, audited, or compared against: the corpus is the provenance of the model. At ~40 MB a
# version it does not belong in git history either, so it is versioned on the Hub instead.
#
# Publish a new version with `hf upload` (see docs/agent/training-agents-runbook.md).
data/corpora/
data/sft-logs/
